   statement: >-
-    The series holds no quantum of the gravitational gauge field (conventions, section ``Gravity and the
-    graviton''), and its registered entanglement prediction treats the field of a body, in the static limit,
-    as an operator built from the matter's commuting numbers
-    (\claimref{field-theory.operator-newtonian-coupling}). At first order the field is fixed by its source at
-    every non-null momentum, and at null momentum two components are not
-    (\claimref{synthesis.gravitational-pair-production-from-the-operator-source-at-first-order}, clause (i)).
-    Decide what the series says of those two components, and whether it requires its gravitational field to
-    commute with the observables of matter at spacelike separation: a condition the store does not state, and
-    which, in a scalar lattice model, a field with no variable of its own fails and a free part with canonical
-    commutators restores
-    (\claimref{synthesis.field-slaved-to-an-operator-source-does-not-commute-at-spacelike-separation}).
+    Restated 18 November, after Leon's decision of that day. The series requires that no signal pass outside the
+    light cone (conventions, section ``Gravity and the graviton'', the requirement of 18 November 2026). In the
+    stored lattice model a field with no variables of its own, slaved to the matter's operator source, fails to
+    commute with the source's later detection at spacelike separation
+    (\claimref{synthesis.field-slaved-to-an-operator-source-does-not-commute-at-spacelike-separation}), and
+    under the hypothesis that a classical device couples to such a field the failure is a signal of first order
+    (\claimref{synthesis.with-a-coupled-device-the-slaved-field-failure-is-a-first-order-signal-and-a-survey-finds-no-stored-bound};
+    its transfer to the gravitational field is argued). So, by that decision, a gravitational field with no
+    variables of its own is not the full account of the field. The series holds no quantum of the gravitational
+    gauge field and posits none. At first order the field is fixed by its source at every non-null momentum; at
+    a null momentum two directions, the transverse trace-free ones, are not, and four of the ten first-order
+    equations are constraints
+    (\claimref{synthesis.first-order-gravitational-field-has-two-free-directions-at-null-momentum-and-four-constraints}).
+    Open: how the requirement is met. Whether the two free directions carry states or variables of their own is
+    not decided, in either sense, and no other way of meeting the requirement is stored. Say how the series'
+    gravitational field meets the requirement, and restate the burst baseline and the stored readings that name
+    a graviton to match.
