+    (18 November, second pass.) A decision and three results. The decision (Leon, 18 November): the series
+    requires no signal outside the light cone, so the slaved field is not the full account of the gravitational
+    field; how the requirement is met is this problem, and no quantum is posited. The field at null momentum
+    (\claimref{synthesis.first-order-gravitational-field-has-two-free-directions-at-null-momentum-and-four-constraints}):
+    at every nonzero null momentum the kernel of the first-order Einstein map is the displacements together with
+    the two transverse trace-free maps (proved); the map is symmetric for the stored pairing, so the first-order
+    equation is solvable there exactly for sources with no transverse trace-free part; the pole of the
+    first-order curvature on the cone lies in those two components only, and the stored bilinear restricted to
+    the cone is a sum of two squares, one for each; four of the ten equations carry no second derivative in the
+    time of a frame, the constraints (all proved); the pseudoscalar exchanges the curvatures of the two
+    directions, so they are one mode over $\mathrm{span}\{1, I_{4}\}$ per null momentum, as for the stored
+    photon (computed). Nothing in it decides whether the series gives those solutions any existence of their
+    own. The lattice Maxwell model, as restated after review
+    (\claimref{synthesis.two-dimensional-lattice-maxwell-coulomb-slaved-field-fails-and-string-dressed-detection-commutes}):
+    a lattice Maxwell field in two space dimensions with a Gauss constraint and a scalar charge, exactly
+    solvable, and not a model of spin two. With no variable of its own the constraint fixes only the divergence
+    of the field: the static slaved field, the Coulomb one, fails to commute with the detection on $76$ of the
+    $82$ links off the string (proved); a string-shaped slaved field satisfies the constraint and commutes off
+    the string at one time, but is not a static solution (proved); with an exact cone the retarded slaved field
+    fails at $878$ of $2750$ spacelike events, every one in the forward cone of the source event and none
+    spacelike to the source (computed); and a slaved field obeying the field equation and fitted to one
+    detection's time commutes with that detection at all spacelike events and fails for a detection at another
+    time (computed for two detection times). With transverse variables and canonical commutators a detection
+    dressed by one Weyl operator commutes with the field exactly off the support of the dressing: the string
+    dressing gives commutation at all $2750$ spacelike events and the Coulomb dressing does not; dressings by
+    sums of such operators are not treated. In one space dimension there is no transverse part and no failure
+    outside the interval between the two sites. For the gravitational field the reading is argued by analogy and
+    settles nothing. The signal
+    (\claimref{synthesis.with-a-coupled-device-the-slaved-field-failure-is-a-first-order-signal-and-a-survey-finds-no-stored-bound}):
+    under its hypothesis (D), that a classical device couples to the field by the model's own coupling with
+    unitary evolution, the stored commutator is a change of the detection probability of first order in the
+    device's strength (proved); its coefficient is nonzero at $172$ of the $502$ spacelike events of the stored
+    grid, and at the $32$ of them not later than the detection the device changes the detection probability
+    (computed). The slaved model with the device is unitary, so unitarity does not imply commutation (proved);
+    with the free part of the stored model the first-order term vanishes (proved). The device is a number, so no
+    floor on localisation hides the signal. Its gravitational size within the light-crossing time is at most
+    $\Phi_{w} = (Gm_{A}m_{B}/\hbar c)\,D\,|1/r_{1} - 1/r_{2}|$, half of that in the formulation that does not
+    count the pair's energy twice (argued, its numbers computed): about $1.3 \times 10^{-13}$ in the proposed
+    experiments, ten orders below the registered threshold, and of order one for a source of about $190$ kg at
+    one metre against a superposed mass of $10^{-14}$ kg. A survey of the stored locality statements and of the
+    cutoff and local-horizon premises, with its scope listed, found none that implies commutation for the
+    gravitational field, none that bounds the failure or makes it unobservable, and no other condition in its
+    place; that is the outcome of a survey, not a theorem about the store.
